PURPOSE:
Demonstrate that each component contributes meaningfully under the specific
attack type it was designed to address (not just under scaling attack).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPERIMENT 1A: Ablation Under GAUSSIAN NOISE INJECTION Attack
(Validates VAE component)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SETUP (identical to existing Table 9 ablation EXCEPT attack type):
  - Dataset:        Alzheimer's MRI (6,983 samples, 4 classes)
  - Clients:        10 total
  - Malicious:      40% (4 malicious clients)
  - Attack:         *** GAUSSIAN NOISE INJECTION, sigma = 15.0 ***
  - Distribution:   Dirichlet alpha = 0.1 (extreme non-IID)
  - Rounds:         25
  - Local epochs:   5-8
  - Batch size:     16
  - Optimizer:      FedBN-P (mu = 0.01)
  - Learning rate:  1e-4, weight decay 5e-5
  - Seed:           42

CONFIGURATIONS TO RUN (5 total):
  1. OptiGradTrust (Full system)
  2. w/o VAE Fingerprinting    (disable VAE reconstruction error signal)
  3. w/o Shapley Values        (disable Shapley computation)
  4. w/o RL Adaptation         (disable DDQN, use attention-only trust)
  5. FedAvg (No Defense)       (uniform aggregation, no trust scoring)

METRICS TO RECORD FOR EACH CONFIGURATION:
  - Final test accuracy (%)
  - Delta Accuracy vs Full system (percentage points)
  - Detection Precision (%)
  - Detection Recall (%)
  - Detection F1 (%)

EXPECTED RESULTS:
  - Removing VAE should cause a NOTICEABLE drop in accuracy or detection
    under noise attack (unlike under scaling where VAE had zero impact),
    because VAE learns the distributional model of benign gradients and
    noise injection pushes gradients off this learned manifold.
  - Shapley should still be important (maybe less than under scaling).
  - RL impact should still be minimal (static attack schedule).

DELIVERABLE FORMAT:
  A table with this structure (same format as existing Table 9):

  Configuration          | Accuracy (%) | Delta Acc | Recall (%) | F1 (%)
  -----------------------|-------------|-----------|------------|--------
  OptiGradTrust (Full)   |             |     --    |            |
  w/o VAE Fingerprinting |             |           |            |
  w/o Shapley Values     |             |           |            |
  w/o RL Adaptation      |             |           |            |
  FedAvg (No Defense)    |             |           |    --      |   --

